.TH PYRA-SOUND 1 "November 2026" "pyra-sound 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pyra-sound \- sound tray icon for the DragonBox Pyra
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyra-sound
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyra-sound
puts a sound icon in MATE's Notification Area, in place of
.BR mate-volume-control-status-icon .
A left click mutes and unmutes the sound. A right click opens a small window
to choose between the speakers and the headphones, with a bar showing the
volume of the output that plays; it closes on a click outside it or on
Escape.
.PP
The icon shows MATE's volume icon on the speakers, a headphones picture on
the headphones, and the muted icon on either when muted. The tooltip names
the output and the amplifier volume, and adds PulseAudio's volume when that
is not 100%.
.PP
The volume wheel is handled by the
.B pyra_volumed
daemon, not by
.BR pyra-sound .
When the running daemon does not drive the headphone amplifier (or none
runs), the right-click window shows a headphone volume slider in place of the
bar while the headphones play.
.PP
.B pyra-sound
runs as the logged-in user and needs no root. It controls the PulseAudio sink
.B aess
through
.BR pactl (1)
and reads the amplifier volumes of the ALSA card
.B L15
with
.BR amixer (1).
It works on the Pyra's AESS kernels (5.6.19-m4*) only; on a kernel with the
direct McPDM audio path it prints
.B unsupported
on standard error and exits with status 0.
.PP
It is normally started at login by
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart/pyra-sound.desktop .
Only one copy runs per session; a second start exits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/pyra-sound.desktop
Starts
.B pyra-sound
with the MATE session.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/pyra/autostart/mate-volume-control-status-icon.desktop
Hides MATE's own sound icon. Removed with the package. To keep MATE's icon
for one user, copy
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/mate-volume-control-status-icon.desktop
into
.IR ~/.config/autostart .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR amixer (1)
